@startuml composite-emission
title US-06: Composite Emission - One Alert Persisted and Pushed, Individual Alerts Suppressed

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Kafka
participant "Express API" as API
database "TimescaleDB\nalerts table" as TSDB
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
actor Operator

Evaluator -> Kafka : publish ONE composite alert\n{ alert_id, type: COMPOSITE,\n  priority: ELEVATED,\n  entity_b: signal loss,\n  entity_a: unrelated proximity,\n  correlation_window_ms,\n  window_start_ms,\n  location, timestamp_ms }

note over Evaluator
  Individual SIGNAL_LOSS and
  UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY alerts
  for this event are NOT emitted.
  The composite replaces both.
end note

Kafka -> API : consume composite alert

API -> TSDB : INSERT INTO alerts\n( alert_id, entity_id, alert_type: COMPOSITE,\n  status: NEW, created_at, payload )\nON CONFLICT (alert_id) DO NOTHING

note over TSDB
  Composite alert stored as a single row.
  alert_id = {entity_id}:COMPOSITE:{window_start_ms}
  Idempotent - safe under Kafka replay.
  Operator can acknowledge and resolve it
  via the same lifecycle flow as any alert (US-13).
end note

TSDB --> API : inserted (or conflict - no-op)

note over API
  Fan-out: check each active WebSocket connection's
  saved scope before pushing.
  geo_region bounds + entity_type + COMPOSITE
  must all match the connection's scope.
end note

API --> Dashboard : push composite alert over WebSocket\n(only to connections whose scope matches)

Dashboard --> Operator : single elevated alert displayed\n(signal loss + proximity correlated)\nstatus: NEW

note over Dashboard, Operator
  Operator sees one notification,
  not two.
  Priority is visually elevated above
  individual signal loss or proximity alerts.
end note

@enduml
